#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Store Qiskit objects to disk so you can continue where you left off"
msgstr "Almacena objetos de Qiskit en disco para continuar donde lo dejaste"

#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Save circuits to disk"
msgstr "Guardar circuitos en disco"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/save-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"guides/save-circuits.ipynb\" />\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/*\n"
"  DO NOT EDIT THIS CELL!!!\n"
"  This cell's content is generated automatically by a script. Anything you add\n"
"  here will be removed next time the notebook is run. To add new content, create\n"
"  a new cell before or after this one.\n"
"*/}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Package versions\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Versiones de paquetes\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"El código de esta página fue desarrollado usando los siguientes requisitos.\n"
"Recomendamos usar estas versiones o versiones más recientes.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Use [QPY serialization](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) to save your circuit to file. QPY files store the full Qiskit circuit object and will be compatible with newer versions of Qiskit (although not necessarily with older versions of Qiskit).\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Usa la [serialización QPY](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qpy) para guardar tu circuito en un archivo. Los archivos QPY almacenan el objeto de circuito completo de Qiskit y serán compatibles con versiones más recientes de Qiskit (aunque no necesariamente con versiones anteriores).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To demonstrate, the following cell creates a simple quantum circuit.\n"
msgstr "Para demostrarlo, la siguiente celda crea un circuito cuántico sencillo.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To save this file to disk, use the `qpy.dump` function. You can also save a list of circuits.\n"
msgstr "Para guardar este archivo en disco, usa la función `qpy.dump`. También puedes guardar una lista de circuitos.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This circuit is now saved to the file `test.qpy`. If you restart your Python kernel, you can re-load the circuit using the `qpy.load` function. Note that this always returns a list of circuits, even if you only serialized one circuit.\n"
msgstr "Este circuito queda guardado en el archivo `test.qpy`. Si reinicias tu kernel de Python, puedes volver a cargar el circuito usando la función `qpy.load`. Ten en cuenta que esta función siempre devuelve una lista de circuitos, incluso si solo serializaste uno.\n"

